y":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the failure-disposition contract for the Gerrit webhook reject arm: what HTTP status/disposition surfaces so Gerrit either redelivery (retryable) or the loss is intentionally fatal-and-alarmed.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.625,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 5: 'keep Gerrit deliveries rejected' and 'accept tokenless Gerrit-originated webhooks only when...'","Step 4 proves only acceptance: 'accepted/queued by /webhook (HTTP 202/no new 401)'","ABSENCE: no disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent) stated for what the rejected Gerrit delivery surfaces to the producer"],"finding":"The plan adds a new auth-rejection arm for Gerrit-originated webhooks (rejected when X-Origin-Url mismatches, an X-Forwarded-For is present, or the TCP peer is not the internal Gerrit host) but never states the DISPOSITION surfaced to the Gerrit producer when that arm fires — whether a rejected delivery is a retryable/transient outcome (Gerrit should redeliver) or a fatal/permanent one. AC4/AC5 only prove the accept path (202/no new 401); the reject path's disposition is unstated, so a future auth break could silently drop deliveries Gerrit never retries.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6b44e80d59b57246","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"RCA plan step 5 / step 4; ACs on internal-origin acceptance and public spoof rejection","norm_id":"nb38307e7fc6aaf5f","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a one-line disposition statement in step 5: e.g. an internal-origin auth reject returns 401 (fatal/permanent — Gerrit will not redeliver) and is the alarmed condition, distinct from transient/queue-full 5xx which stay retryable so Gerrit redeliveries.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the rejection counter increment and the observability publish-then-reset are atomic against concurrent webhook deliveries (no lost-update / TOCTOU), not only durable across restarts.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC10: 'without losing increments across review-bot restarts or failed CloudWatch publishes'","ABSENCE: no statement that the increment and the publish-then-reset are atomic (lock/CAS) against concurrent deliveries — only restart/failed-publish persistence is addressed"],"finding":"The webhook auth-rejection counter is shared mutable state incremented on every rejected delivery and read by /health and published per-interval by observability.sh; the plan specifies restart/reset persistence (AC10) but does not state the concurrency/atomicity of the increment under concurrent webhook deliveries (check-then-act / lost-update risk when multiple rejections and a CloudWatch publish-and-reset interleave).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd92e7d76771b0376","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC10 'reviewbot_webhook_auth_rejections without losing increments across review-bot restarts or failed CloudWatch publishes'; step 5 'expose auth rejections via health + CloudWatch'","norm_id":"n810113a30854c9b5","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Ground the X-Origin-Url capability claim in the actual deployed Gerrit 3.14 webhooks plugin source/JAR (cite the class/method that adds the header and confirm it is not client-settable) before treating the header identity as established in the fix and docs; if unconfirmed, keep Gerrit deliveries rejected per step 2's own gate rather than asserting the header in steps 4/5/7 and the ACs.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6717,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 2: 'The observed plugin header is Gerrit's built-in X-Origin-Url'","Plan step 5: 'accept tokenless Gerrit-originated webhooks only when the verified X-Origin-Url matches configured Gerrit URLs'","Retrieved Gerrit webhooks plugin config docs (gerrit.googlesource.com/plugins/webhooks config.md; GerritCodeReview/plugins_webhooks) list remote.NAME.url/event/connectionTimeout/socketTimeout/maxTries/retryInterval/sslVerify but no header emission and no X-Origin-Url","Web results surface X-Origin-Url only as a reverse-proxy/CDN header and as a cache-poisoning attack input (f5.pm 'Demystifying Web Cache Threats'; nginx reverse-proxy config), i.e. a client/proxy-settable header rather than a Gerrit-plugin-authenticated one","Repo infra/gerrit/webhooks.config asserts the plugin 'adds its built-in X-Origin-Url header' but cites only ADR-0014, not the plugin source/JAR"],"finding":"The plan's load-bearing capability assertion — that the Gerrit webhooks plugin emits a built-in `X-Origin-Url` request header usable as an auth signal — is not corroborated by retrievable prior art; the plugin's documented config exposes no header-emission feature, and `X-Origin-Url` in general web practice is a proxy/CDN/attacker-influenced header (including a documented cache-poisoning vector), which undercuts using it as an authentication signal.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff09157abd15ae9f0","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"RCA plan step 2 and step 5; Acceptance Criteria lines 2-4 and the spoof-rejection AC","norm_id":"n5a9aa434e286e663","priority":0.1283,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The deployed 3.14 webhooks plugin does not emit X-Origin-Url (or emits a differently-named header), so the tokenless path never matches and Gerrit deliveries stay rejected after shipping","An attacker or intermediary who can reach the receiver sets X-Origin-Url themselves, since it is a commonly spoofable proxy header, weakening the auth even with the peer/XFF checks"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a step-2 sub-task that records the concrete plugin class/method emitting the header (e.g. the webhooks plugin's HTTP session/post code path) and the exact header name observed in a redacted live capture, and rephrase steps 4/5/7 and the ACs to treat the header identity as verified-from-source rather than assumed; additionally justify why X-Origin-Url is safe as an auth signal despite being a conventionally proxy/client-settable header, relying on the peer-resolution + XFF-absence checks rather than the header alone.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"no","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"13ffb4066b539313","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["1f789cded6eea7b7",4563],"description_boxes"